# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/fusion-2 window (the prefill levers on the ship stack: the prefill SDPA with one q chunk per core, WPP, and the 13x10 matmul grids, M1; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-6 is the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (the oneq lever needs its binary; every arm without the flag runs that binary with the lever off). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# DC1 (TIMED, the DECODE ABAB proving no decode loss, first pair): the CONTROL (A1): the combined fusion arm itself; eight live (concurrent8_steady) in the first pair of
# the ABAB, every boot a fresh reset. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. READ:
# c2_smoke_check clean (a lever boot also has its engaged lines and no fell-back line), no stall; then PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians: python3
# scripts/ci/w2ln_timing_compare.py pair <A container log> <B container log> --window steady --a-smoke <A smoke log> --b-smoke <B smoke log> for (DC1, DL1) and (DC2, DL2),
# and its floor subcommand over the two control logs; the texts equal (text_mismatches empty) and the accepted prefixes equal. The oneq lever acts only in prefill, so it
# cannot move a decode round; the grid13 verify and drafter sub-switches DO act in decode (the verify block's output projections, the fused commit's feature projection;
# est. under 0.6 ms of a ~125 ms round, inside the control-to-control floor). The GO rule of this ABAB is therefore NO LOSS: the lever's round time not above the control's
# beyond the floor, in both pairs. A loss is a NO-GO for the grid13 verify or drafter sub-switch (re-run with QWEN_FAST_GRID13=prefill, a twin profile of
# fusion-wp/M1.json), never a reason to drop the prefill gain. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a
# second through the smoke step (AICLK and the limiter holding it, power, current, temperature); read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result, and the first
# [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. It runs on the host and is not part of any arm; it is on every leg so the pairs stay paired. A gain that comes with a different
# loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. Duration (estimate): 35 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-6
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
